  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499423538378_387250_26990" xmi:uuid="0d5d051f-05a7-4001-a3a2-3c5072dd991f" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8e001ed_1510149807888_304354_31098" xmi:uuid="0fc0c92f-43e4-4456-9627-33a8fd53383e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499423538378_387250_26990"/>
      <body>This capability enables the representation of detailed assembly information on how the involved part occurences are mated together and which constraints apply. &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A MatingDefinition is a kind of AssemblyDefinition with additionnal mating information.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;A MatedPartRelationship defines how two MatedPartAssociations of a MatingDefinition are mated together. The type of mating and auxiliary mating materials can be specified.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;An AssemblyShapeJoint provides detailed information on how two or more ShapeElements of Occurrences in an AssemblyDefinition are joined using AssemblyShapeJointItemRelationship.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;An AssemblyShapeConstraint provides detailed information on how two or more ShapeElements of Occurrences in an AssemblyDefinition are geometrically constrained against each others using AssemblyShapeConstraintItemRelationship.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;Mating_domainModel_Overview.png&lt;/name&gt;Simplified overview of the AP242 mating Domain model&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
    </ownedComment>
    <name>Mating</name>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1502117423446_167948_36361" xmi:uuid="012c103e-7522-4871-b47e-6595c222b35b" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1512401005601_113245_41587" xmi:uuid="48a70593-d486-461a-9c4d-74bd6f7c3856" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1502117423446_167948_36361"/>
        <body>An AssemblyShapeJointItemRelationship is a type of ShapeElementRelationship that relates an OccurrenceShapeFeature into an AssemblyShapeJoint. </body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>AssemblyShapeJointItemRelationship</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1512401106065_379306_41590" xmi:uuid="9f2b3e0b-411a-4626-8dc6-8e1c2b38f16a" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1722423547803_72214_141406" xmi:uuid="8942aa55-25e8-4613-a853-87febdb5751e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1722423559534_452411_141407" xmi:uuid="b178238e-eed8-4352-9cba-db6ad851c53b" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>&lt;sch:rule context="//ShapeElementRelationship[@uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='AssemblyShapeJointItemRelationship']"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="partView1" value="ancestor::PartView"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="relatedOccurrenceShapeFeatureRef" value="Related/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="occurrenceShapeFeature" value="//*[@uid=$relatedOccurrenceShapeFeatureRef and local-fn:testXsiTypeOccurrenceShapeFeature(@xsi:type)=true()]"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="topOccurrence" value="if (count($occurrenceShapeFeature/ancestor::Occurrence[@uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='SpecifiedOccurrence']) = 0) then $occurrenceShapeFeature/ancestor::Occurrence[@uid]/@uid else local-fn:MainUpperUsage(//DataContainer, $occurrenceShapeFeature/ancestor::Occurrence[@uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='SpecifiedOccurrence'][position()=1]/@uid)"&gt;&lt;/sch:let&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="local-fn:testXsiTypeAssemblyDefinition($partView1/@xsi:type)=true() and (some $j in //PartView[child::ViewOccurrenceRelationship[substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='NextAssemblyOccurrenceUsage']/Related/@uidRef=$topOccurrence] satisfies ($j eq $partView1) and local-fn:testXsiTypeAssemblyDefinition($j/@xsi:type)=true())"&gt;(AssemblyShapeJointItemRelationship_WR1 &lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt;) following two paths starting from the related and relating attributes shall end in the same instance of AssemblyDefinition. The first AssemblyDefinition ( &lt;sch:value-of select="$partView1/@uid"/&gt; ) is reached by following the ElementOf of the Relating AssemblyShapeJoint. The second AssemblyDefinition is reached by following the ElementOf of the Related OccurrenceShapeFeature ( &lt;sch:value-of select="$occurrenceShapeFeature/@uid"/&gt; ) through an optional chain of SpecifiedOccurrence to a top Occurrence ( &lt;sch:value-of select="$topOccurrence"/&gt; ) that is used in the AssemblyDefinition ( &lt;sch:value-of select="//PartView[child::ViewOccurrenceRelationship/Related/@uidRef=$topOccurrence]/@uid "/&gt; ) by a NextAssemblyOccurrenceUsage ( &lt;sch:value-of select="//ViewOccurrenceRelationship[Related/@uidRef=$topOccurrence]/@uid "/&gt; ).&lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1512401225909_775798_41594" xmi:uuid="f14c7472-18af-4b3e-a60e-952091d96032" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1512401106065_379306_41590"/>
          <body>following two paths starting from the related and relating attributes shall end in the same instance of AssemblyDefinition. The first AssemblyDefinition is reached by following the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_Mating.htm#AssemblyShapeJoint.ElementOf&lt;/path&gt; ElementOf&lt;/a&gt; of the Relating AssemblyShapeJoint. The second AssemblyDefinition is reached by following the &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_ElectricalHarness.htm#OccurrenceShapeFeature.ElementOf&lt;/path&gt; ElementOf&lt;/a&gt; of the Related OccurrenceShapeFeature through an optional chain of SpecifiedOccurrence to a top Occurrence that is used in the AssemblyDefinition by a NextAssemblyOccurrenceUsage.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1502117423446_167948_36361"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1512401106067_375387_41591" xmi:uuid="a244eaf8-bb8e-48c5-aeba-8a9055d6b538" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.Relating-&gt;closure(ElementOf)-&gt;select(e | e.ElementOf.oclIsUndefined()) = self.Related-&gt;closure(ElementOf)-&gt;select(e | e.ElementOf.oclIsUndefined()) </body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1502117529803_353046_36455" xmi:uuid="28967034-6da3-45a6-b9af-a132d55e0594" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general href="../ShapeAssociationAndStructure/ShapeAssociationAndStructure.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193244_138840_23841"/>
      </generalization>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1502117631770_930348_36517" xmi:uuid="0f929acb-15a4-483b-a9ad-8d843c934255" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1512401028382_33662_41588" xmi:uuid="06460e83-5214-4312-9240-5ed32a28ec22" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1502117631770_930348_36517"/>
          <body>an inherited attribute that shall be of type AssemblyShapeJoint. </body>
        </ownedComment>
